<title>USA: American Business Products Q4 net drops.</title>
<headline>American Business Products Q4 net drops.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Condensed Consolidated Income Statements</p>
<p>	    (Dollars in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>				December 31,	  December 31,</p>
<p>			   1996	 1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Net Sales	  $159,244   $162,977    $631,638    $633,955</p>
<p>Cost of Goods Sold</p>
<p>			 111,589    115,642     443,621     447,375</p>
<p>Selling and</p>
<p>Administrative</p>
<p>  Expenses	    36,022     35,185     142,229     139,536</p>
<p>Restructuring Charges</p>
<p>			   2,535	  ---	 8,334	   ---</p>
<p> Total		 150,146    150,827     594,184     586,911</p>
<p> Operating Income    9,098     12,150	37,454	47,044</p>
<p>Other Income (Expense)</p>
<p>Interest Expense</p>
<p>			 (2,073)    (1,769)     (7,525)     (8,243)</p>
<p>Miscellaneous -- net</p>
<p>			     429	1,132	 4,110	 2,701</p>
<p>Income before Income Taxes  </p>
<p>			   7,454     11,513	34,039	41,502</p>
<p>Provision for Income Taxes</p>
<p>			   2,573	3,913	12,985	15,997</p>
<p> Net income	    4,881	7,600	21,054	25,505</p>
<p>Earnings per common share</p>
<p>			     .29	  .46	  1.28	  1.57</p>
<p>Average number of common</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>		   16,405,219  16,374,366  16,395,851  16,197,044</p>
<p>		    (Unaudited)</p>
<p>NOTE: Fourth quarter 1996 results include restructuring charge of $2,535,000 before income taxes and, included in Miscellaneous Other Income, gains of $1,721,000 before income taxes upon sale of realty rendered redundant by the restructuring and a loss of $2,786,000 before income taxes on the Vanier sale. These factors reduced fourth quarter 1996 net income by $1,976,000, or $0.12 per share.  Without them, the Company would have shown fourth quarter 1996 net income of $6,857,000 or $0.42 per share.</p>
<p>Full year 1996 results include a restructuring charge of $8,334,000, related realty gains of $3,129,000 and the Vanier sale loss of $2,786,000, all expressed before income taxes.  These factors reduced 1996 net income by $4,573,000, or $0.28 per share.  Without them the Company would have shown 1996 net income of $25,627,000 or $1.56 per share. SOURCE  American Business Products</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
